==Trivia==
*The name Idi may be derived from ''ID'', ''[[wikipedia:Id, ego and superego|id]]'', ''[[wikipedia:Eden|Eden]]'', 遺伝 ''iden'' (genetic heredity), アイディア ''aidia'' (idea), アイディアル ''aidiaru'' (ideal), or アイディリック ''aidirikku'' (idyllic).
*"Ne" may be derived from 根 ''ne'' (a plant's root; the root of or cause or basis for something; the nature one has from birth), ''new'' (referring to her being a new form of Idi, creating new Idis by reproducing, or [[Master of Life Dr. Nova (Special Cat)|Nova]]'s name being Latin for "new") ''next'' (referring to how she is the next step in [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N]]'s evolution line), ''nexus'' (a connected group, like the Idi:Nes in [[The Face of God/Invasion|The Face of God Invasion]]), or 猫 ''neko'' (cat).
*"Unstable microbes detected" appears to be a mistranslation. Idi:Ne's Japanese description has a space between 不安定 ''fuantei'' (unstable) and 古ノ微生物検出 ''ko no biseibutsu kenshutsu'' (paleobacteria detected), implying that these are two separate assessments: Idi:Ne is unstable, and paleobacteria is detected on her.
*"Reproduces by saving and spreading seeds" may be another mistranslation, as the kanji 種 can mean both "seed" and "species", 保存 ''hozon'' means "conservation" or "preservation", and 増殖 ''zōshoku'' means "multiplication" or "propagation". Overall, it may have been meant as "reproduces to preserve the species."
**However, [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relics]]' tree-like designs and the [[Media:Bg228.png |Relic trees]] seen in The Face of God Invasion could point to the seed/species ambiguity being deliberate.
*The master mentioned in Idi:Ne's Japanese description is likely [[Sage of Life Dr. Nova]], whose own Japanese description says she wants to create perfect life.
**This would mean Dr. Nova's attempts at perfect life were her own undoing, as [[Revival of Origin/Invasion|Revival of Origin Invasion]] appears to have been designed specifically to be cleared with Idi:NX.
*In Japanese, Idi:Ne and [[Idi:Re]] have very different descriptions from other enemies, using exclusively kanji and katakana, even for words that would normally be spelled using hiragana.
*She has a higher ID than Sage of Life Dr. Nova despite requiring less progress to encounter.
*She was added in [[Version 13.7 Update|Version 13.7]] on September 26th, 2024, exactly 49 months after Idi:Re was added ([[Version 9.9 Update|Version 9.9]] on August 26th, 2020). This length of time may be a reference to how 49 is the number of sub-chapters in [[Stories of Legend]] and [[Uncanny Legends]].
*Idi:Ne spawning many times throughout The Face of God Invasion may be because [[Elder Flame Doron]], the main enemy of the original [[The Face of God]], was also spawned repeatedly.
**The Face of God may have also been chosen for her stage because [[Laboratory of Relics]] and [[Ancient Forest Labyrinth]] share the same map image, along with a couple other sub-chapters.

